<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Russian strikes kill several in Kyiv region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0760d1425d8eb2e4f4543cd946deca8900b8100d72e3a145d99e8d7ce8d9bb73</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T07:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russian-strikes-kill-several-in-kyiv-region/live-80015859--26d9dc409d7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russian-strikes-kill-several-in-kyiv-region/live-80015859?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Overnight attacks claimed the lives of civilians in the Kyiv region. Also, NATO is set to discuss Russian violations of Polish airspace. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Metalworkers go on strike as pay dispute heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bed514248cb5150da7f4a05577f283bf859fb8ede53ee7af88f153cc2e7939e8</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633--a1790c046188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest union is calling for more strikes over heated pay disputes with car makers like Mercedes and shipyards among the companies impacted. Meanwhile, a Berlin hospital fire leaves many injured. Follow DW.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Is rule-breaking contagious? The bad apple effect explained</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:158084693ec0388d790e43a1e0438f0ba06ea6fc8f86dcc3599ed2a4cfeedc5a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-rule-breaking-contagious-the-bad-apple-effect-explained/a-79980025--2bf7f79ae276.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-rule-breaking-contagious-the-bad-apple-effect-explained/a-79980025?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seeing someone break a rule makes people more likely to break it too, a new study finds, especially when the rule-breaker is on their side politically. Watching others behave well barely made a difference.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Thousands protest closure of critical media outlets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d30a3d236e047a58eee3109df7222c6c1379c69969ecabc77ab723a98143bac</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T21:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-thousands-protest-closure-of-critical-media-outlets/a-80015347--7bbb07b22139.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-thousands-protest-closure-of-critical-media-outlets/a-80015347?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protesters gathered in Istanbul to show their support for press freedom in Turkey. The protest was called just days after the police raided Sozcu TV and arrested several senior staff members.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan: Drones hit UN building, residential area in Khartoum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a37e46de4e7539019920afe7181b0aa47144ff9558d280c1db5dde06d462f72</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T19:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drones-hit-un-building-residential-area-in-khartoum/a-80015122--86bdbc88b2b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drones-hit-un-building-residential-area-in-khartoum/a-80015122?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The drones targeted Khartoum, damaging a UN building in the residential area. The UN agency deemed it unacceptable that humanitarian workers were exposed to such danger.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Libya: Suspected drone attack hits Russian ship in Benghazi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:050e4db268a1cb64dcbdd1cb8c27ba06503052a286e7206788e90c29227c312b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/libya-suspected-drone-attack-hits-russian-ship-in-benghazi/a-80014545--a60ea6375dca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/libya-suspected-drone-attack-hits-russian-ship-in-benghazi/a-80014545?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Russian vessel at an eastern Libyan naval base was hit by what is suspected to be a drone strike.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Eisenkot condemns 'Jewish terrorism' in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18272f74ede258247c0e29018ee9b4a41e319ce0bc002897720159a41b2955a8</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-s-eisenkot-condemns-jewish-terrorism-in-west-bank/a-80013861--f4c08d0b63d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-eisenkot-condemns-jewish-terrorism-in-west-bank/a-80013861?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has condemned a recent series of arson attacks in the occupied West Bank as "Jewish terrorism." Israeli authorities have opened an investigation into the incidents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 climate talks end without consensus on how to fund vulnerable countries or move the world away from coal, oil and gas use</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b41dc6d71600421f62e5dee5bd35aa2a73dc2171c59de8707a8735f8282f491</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away/a-80003610--d912dc284aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away-from-coal-oil-and-gas-use/a-80003610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two weeks of tough talks, the COP31 climate summit has closed without a consensus on how to quit fossil fuels or fund countries struggling to adapt to a hotter world.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Climate deal 'not adopted,' summit president says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7333ba6a5a5bb562bcf545131e5f28bacfa166e4448b5cdfae9170bf76e570fb</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T12:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-deal-not-adopted-summit-president-says/live-79999516--d760f7d7f78d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-deal-not-adopted-summit-president-says/live-79999516?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summit was extended as nations worked to reach a deal, but they couldn't agree on including fossil fuels. European nations, small island states and activists have criticized oil-producing countries for the impasse.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich bosses under fire over Jamal Musiala comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1c5b4eb9b8acbc45077254824011aba1f9e933824763efa312cdd6680d10556</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187--78383bcfae5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Officials have publicly questioned whether Musiala will ever fully recover from a debilitating neurological condition and queried the validity of his contract, prompting criticism from fans, media and the FIFPRO union.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China, ASEAN countries struggle over South China Sea code of conduct</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a3f8142478d3911d8b84647b109c9a7254025e7acf7d35ef7988cbc9580c312</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799--a3492edf3810.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Philippines wanted a South China Sea code of conduct in place by 2026. But persistent disagreements between China and ASEAN countries are slowing progress toward a deal.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Inspired by Bernie Sanders: A German agency is using US-Style campaigning to boost the left in 2029</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9896ff646f6aee10f98d1ffa60578e00bf9fafb1c606e2b41df1f6f5a4511f64</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443--f6cd4061ee72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"The Goodforces" wants to see a swing to the left in the 2029 German elections. The agency counts New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani and Bernie Sanders among its inspirations. Could it transform the political landscape?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: IG Metall union calls for new 24-hour strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06468981b17a05acd9fdaa3552a926ddf2479846645f620e697d507780b4fc1a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430--32c896775229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest single union, IG Metall, is calling on car and shipyard workers to strike amid a pay row. Meanwhile, Germany's president is setting off on an Africa trip. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: ICE arrests 2 at Seattle airport in 'chilling' scenes — governor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb3ebefe14f1ddfb3b1e4039f52fafa7dde211eead1a32479ef2932800534e58</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T07:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-ice-arrests-2-at-seattle-airport-in-chilling-scenes-governor/a-80012480--94de32aa4552.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-ice-arrests-2-at-seattle-airport-in-chilling-scenes-governor/a-80012480?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Washington's governor has denounced the arrests made by ICE officers at Seattle's airport, calling the incident "horrific."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Nepal PM Balendra Shah heads to Delhi for first bilateral visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5f5f85f7de5e9483724a63c2b2fd4222f6016cea3f1dbacd0ba7360a9184628</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104--4f17524b4e9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rapper-turned-prime minister Balendra Shah is in New Delhi for his first foreign bilateral trip since taking office. He is expected to discuss flood recovery, trade and energy in his talks with Modi. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens missing as deadly fire hits Indonesian candy factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bee494b645342de89d32a2651e01ba46c601e60c7e43be6cfcd38ad92fc9924d</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342--07c7cd5dbdea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least three people were killed in a devastating fire at a confectionery factory on Java. Officials said many more people remain unaccounted for, prompting fears of a much larger tragedy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: At least 24 dead after boat capsizes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aa0bddb7fd5108336f834050550aa6c7cd04b18ccc6eb099d105032516f8f8b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T23:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-at-least-24-dead-after-boat-capsizes/a-80011248--a7e001c6016b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-at-least-24-dead-after-boat-capsizes/a-80011248?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The boat carrying mourners for a funeral overturned in southern Nigeria. It was the latest in a series of deadly boat accidents in the country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Getting rid of antibiotic resistance: Challenges and possible solutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:996179f185d74aed2eb9bb869b88e5efc08ed29efb4122716d7eec04ad3e159a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T18:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/getting-rid-of-antibiotic-resistance-challenges-and-possible-solutions/a-80010693--ca5fce49b0a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/getting-rid-of-antibiotic-resistance-challenges-and-possible-solutions/a-80010693?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">If antibiotics stop working, even the smallest infection can be fatal. The WHO expects millions of deaths over the next 25 years. Can the "One Health" approach help combat antibiotic resistance?</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Mexican special forces arrest drug kingpin 'Chapo Isidro'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21fbc97039d564093a546c7274d77c6f455ecc97d25d9efecf12f77f3617b06f</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T18:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mexican-special-forces-arrest-drug-kingpin-chapo-isidro/a-80010745--0adb20796144.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mexican-special-forces-arrest-drug-kingpin-chapo-isidro/a-80010745?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The alleged leader of the Beltran Leyva gang and one of the FBI's most wanted fugitives, known as "Chapo Isidro," was captured by the Mexican military following a raid and a shootout in the coastal state of Sinaloa.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russian helicopter suspected of violating Finnish airspace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e8c0504cc5dcb9269ad7154b3b6842960e14ae64c1ac91714bbabfcba5d0753</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-helicopter-suspected-of-violating-finnish-airspace/a-80010133--74b233a91706.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-helicopter-suspected-of-violating-finnish-airspace/a-80010133?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland's Defense Ministry thinks the incursion is linked to a drone strike earlier Saturday on a Russian cargo ship, which is on a US sanctions list.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU and Indonesia sign trade deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a41e3f9b89cfca26429fa1910ef400ba539a6c798cb031099b3c5a5b2f685bd0</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099--bb068ad239d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A deal covering 730 million people promises lower tariffs and new investment opportunities as the European Union seeks to diversify trade ties amid growing global economic tensions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New EU budget proposal aims at tax gobal tech giants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f3f0f8e80cf844b8f177a001f311e6df2b07b1b33f8c9f268e25040c38b1d7f</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-eu-budget-proposal-aims-at-tax-gobal-tech-giants/a-80009255--8ff3ddfff270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-eu-budget-proposal-aims-at-tax-gobal-tech-giants/a-80009255?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Council President Antonio Costa has proposed a smaller EU budget for 2028-2034, including a 3% tax on major digital firms to ease member states' contributions. France has already rejected the plan as inadequate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes Zelenskyy's hometown, killing 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05a9d81b5026170729d1f9a2a3c769bc588e8d21ac2824252c12ed98b156b6b7</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458--1c5b88d83c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The attacks follow Russian President Vladimir Putin's vow of a "painful" response to Ukraine's attacks this week on the Kerch Bridge, linking Russian-occupied Crimea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's religious freedom report: Authoritarian regimes, holy wars, and spies abroad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a16d6db2357542dd5e4ebf6f4558b86afd8d5dd19722fc4611d6655476309c3</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-religious-freedom-report-authoritarian-regimes-holy-wars-and-spies-abroad/a-79995216--a4dc5259a9cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-religious-freedom-report-authoritarian-regimes-holy-wars-and-spies-abroad/a-79995216?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Harassment, persecution, surveillance: Across much of the world, people of faith are facing growing pressure. A new German government report is unusually direct in criticizing China in particular.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russian ornithologist jailed over small donations to Navalny's foundation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c9b805c65a2ea023ac724b457aaec8d46ceec07474c24ca17148873cb18aadc</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505--49dba4e1f94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sofia Rosenfeld has devoted her life to studying Arctic birds. A Russian court sentenced her to 3.5 years in a penal colony over donations to Navalny's foundation. Friends and family are fighting for her release.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: No agreement on climate science, disinformation spreading</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d64de87007fe55bd7900ddc85436878b69fa1a3ddfe2dd435c8b287233a16c83</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-no-agreement-on-climate-science-disinformation-spreading/a-80004894--cd9d23743160.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-no-agreement-on-climate-science-disinformation-spreading/a-80004894?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Attacks on climate science and disinformation risk delaying key measures at COP31 in Antalya. As the UN climate talks draw to a close, how will that affect efforts to come to an agreement?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da13b720fb87686aee7efa75ba6cf2badca341c71b827c959e47adfe6c6e580a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098--4f23b2ccbfc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The depiction of the birth of the goddess Athena above the Parthenon's entrance is considered a masterpiece of ancient art. Now, a German research team has pieced together all the surviving fragments.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Better educated than ever — yet Germany's Gen Z is being shut out of its own future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a51f98fb6ffd49b1e5fae0d4e495329e3e42fc279c0ab9e70dac3cdb7a77540c</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/better-educated-than-ever-yet-germany-s-gen-z-is-being-shut-out-of-its-own-future/a-80005823--59d88b978f2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/better-educated-than-ever-yet-germany-s-gen-z-is-being-shut-out-of-its-own-future/a-80005823?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Never before have young people around the world been so well-educated while facing so many economic challenges. Young Germans are asking: Will I be better off than my parents?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Can German auto manufacturing recover after Mercedes and VW cuts?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11728992ce4be3c812c9397297053397cb64751321db3ab0913431809e5ec7c4</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928--88277c189f1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German automakers are pulling back on investments at home, sparking fresh anxiety about the auto sector's future. Some industry watchers think there is still a narrow window to stem the decline. But how?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Measles in America: Here's a constructive approach to beating the disease, based on Brazil's experience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12fc00cd1eecafced674722fa7058996710a8b7145905ac3e6b7346a63b97b76</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/measles-in-america-here-s-a-constructive-approach-to-beating-the-disease-based-on-brazil-s-experienc/a-79990626--11abc405874e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/measles-in-america-here-s-a-constructive-approach-to-beating-the-disease-based-on-brazil-s-experience/a-79990626?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is now officially a measles contagion zone. By mid-2026, there were more infections than in all of the previous year. But the country could beat measles again, just like Brazil did two years ago.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany face Belgium in Nations League quarterfinals — Klopp plays down favorites tag</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1db844ce1501fb60009135100f7f1600b175cbaf52900385092ee4755766adfc</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updat