1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest in a series of raids and arrests, another major pro-opposition Turkish broadcaster has been brought under state control. This is the third in a year.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e993c89aaf71d442578c2cf50f0890e711373e7a05fd994ddfe393f2a57fa7c7</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Lufthansa to cut 1,000 jobs, citing ongoing losses — reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73a9b2b11567ab496b3daead5ae5406326110b4f3a15a07e11e70d333ee8623b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062--a7b4260396ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a letter obtained by the media, Lufthansa's executive board said the German company is losing €20 million every month. In addition to job cuts, operational cuts are also planned.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Have we missed our chance to stop climate change?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f03d9c03c2c9cd96843e7029817c55ca96888fe4fc96930b6b0fc075976e428b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199--68173e73a2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From record-breaking heat to devastating floods and wildfires, the warning signs are everywhere. Can rising temperatures still be brought under control?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Putin proposes second humanitarian ceasefire — is it a trap?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1f52c1a7cab42e331837de2d460c084712cc838d7bacd57a5b8a52975b30873</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772--e715071e3f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian President Putin has suggested evacuating civilians from the embattled Ukrainian city of Kostiantynivka. But experts warn this could serve military, not humanitarian, aims. What should Kyiv do?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda minister at COP31: 'We need a just transition'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75e34f38f9396b2e2f8500823819af4aa67008c44f71bb559c01ce95534c8201</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209--312e033bb073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Funding from wealthy countries to help deal with the impacts of climate change hasn't materialized, says Uganda's environment minister. The East African country is hoping oil and carbon credits will help boost finances.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>No mention of fossil fuels in latest COP31 draft deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2374ac1151e7f23e51e70aa6462702c179c17b7c35c31a686bb901b1fd2fbc76</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-mention-of-fossil-fuels-in-latest-cop31-draft-deal/a-79992394--36cfb19df8f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-mention-of-fossil-fuels-in-latest-cop31-draft-deal/a-79992394?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of the most fraught debates at the UN climate talks in Turkey has revolved around the future of coal, oil and gas. Now, all mention of fossil fuels has been removed from the summit's new draft agreement.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic trading tests investors' appetite for AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a02b931fb70f439bd460fad9bdbff91f26bdfc6b813991938690422a7d4a37d</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163--d18c2700770b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anthropic was valued at $2 trillion after shares started trading on the Nasdaq following a record $81 billion IPO. Its performance will put investor confidence in AI to the test.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Zverev faces fresh lawsuit from ex-girlfriend</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec5290bebefe258bbc8c16c2caf4666bb5b4a400753e5bf2cac281c95a14ec63</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005--d63dbeaa4aae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World No. 1 tennis player Alexander Zverev is facing a new lawsuit related to a domestic abuse trial. The lawyer for his ex-girlfriend, Brenda Patea, told DW what the allegations are against the German player.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU Commission confirms it was targeted in cyberattack using AI tools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f93ec71336ad88dce92239ab2a06b4dd58c93096e2b13f648eafe4d89f05a20</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016--2e1cd85b257c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission was targeted by an "AI-generated cybercampaign," a spokesperson has said. This is the first time the bloc has publicly reported an AI-based cyberattack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wadephul: 'Coalition of the Willing' talks in Berlin send strong signal to Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa1d92da5d9f4823d3487821a9b9da14b3fca1bf20335616ceab4e5769bd4deb</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664--ce1ce93ebd6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Wadephul has said the Coalition of the Willing meeting in Berlin sends a clear message to Moscow to take peace talks seriously. He also warned Ukraine should be prepared for peace talks to fail.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran balances ties with China and Russia as Trump ramps up pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a83322918f75f468167b04c591dc33d90c939b7ee18ca0ac7d5bca983f62be7b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920--3c92417b16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Donald Trump seeks to tighten economic pressure on Iran, China remains its biggest oil customer and Russia a key partner. But both powers are balancing support for Tehran against broader interests with Washington.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48a412ed91a48a629e68db30c22960227c24f4a67516e381fd917d2fb4bb14ac</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms and the Nvidia scandal has cast doubt on Anthropic's IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund bows to fan pressure and end Rheinmetall deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4f39f07a510f56a9a47a288417de94d7d41dcb2bc842219d33a47fbd9313a59</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121--2c9b64a964f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Borussia Dortmund has reluctantly ended its association with a major sponsor after long-term fan protests. They are not the first Bundesliga club to u-turn, as commercial interests clash with politics and fan culture.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>'Coalition of the Willing' meets in Berlin: Europe remains committed to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3930016df5419612ec1f079beac48cf1683a3134ce50e18048aff1ca80e1e56</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996--9529e6865e8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "Coalition of the Willing" supporting Ukraine is gathering in Berlin. One of the key issues under discussion is whether Europe will be able to play a role in future negotiations over the country's future.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How a green economy could help reverse climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e043ed9c0ddbf4d1fdd68bfaab62ed4d2084d70113bce2043bf3494845224e95</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-green-economy-could-help-reverse-climate-change/a-79874576--23cc55e56fdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-green-economy-could-help-reverse-climate-change/a-79874576?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Green growth promises a future in which economies thrive without destroying the environment. But is this vision realistic?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Hashim Thaci's second conviction in The Hague reignites debate in Kosovo about justice and the Kosovo Specialist Chambers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62ca4d58f95e9441afda71ec173e5e553225f117848b93ec1226608750573f7c</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T20:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosov/a-79975227--3db3936546e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosovo-specialist-chambers/a-79975227?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former President Hashim Thaci has been convicted of trying to influence witnesses in his war crimes trial. The conviction has reignited debate in Kosovo about the Kosovo Specialist Chambers, the court that convicted him.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Back to 1997: Russia wants NATO to roll back its eastern expansion</title><id>urn:rssy