l="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In April, about 60 countries held an unprecedented meeting in Colombia to work out a plan to slowly quit oil, coal and gas. How influential is this coalition at the COP31 climate summit?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>AI in classrooms: Fighting the great 'dumbing down'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa7833a5524fcee963cddb881abab70db2e98852583967da096706265f4fd5eb</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T07:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-in-classrooms-fighting-the-great-dumbing-down/a-79949229--354992b7f6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-in-classrooms-fighting-the-great-dumbing-down/a-79949229?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Research suggests that students who aren't careful about how they use ChatGPT and other AI tools risk poorer academic outcomes. It's a huge challenge for teachers.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German economy returns to growth, so why is the country still worried?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b5e6ff89cb0362b2a22fc2899bc5ab1665eda24c1ecded231fcb0b123fe8845</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220--24d2aa1d0aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German economy is growing again, albeit slightly. However, economists warn that without reforms, higher productivity and solid public finances, a loss of prosperity and growing debt threaten future generations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Despite restrictive abortion laws, Poland's 'Abortomat' — a locker that dispenses abortion pills — helps women who want to end a pregnancy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9dab51e130b84f738cf9f7ec580bdae7d3e844b56275f21688628401369e73c</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polish-activists-face-opposition-as-they-make-abortion-more-accessible/a-79943914--39db4083c558.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/despite-restrictive-abortion-laws-poland-s-abortomat-a-locker-that-dispenses-abortion-pills-helps-women-who-want-to-end-a-pregnancy/a-79943914?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abortion laws in Poland are very restrictive. Activists there have found a new way to help women wanting to terminate a pregnancy: the "Abortomat," a locker that dispenses abortion pills. But they face fierce opposition.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Germany holds national day of remembrance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d7b22f420b2ee4f2c2cb8f8897cabf926d5bba7c3ac0f8610c470c3e2f25b5</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500--7252f2ee958f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Events were held for "Volkstrauertag," a day commemorating victims of war and oppression. Meanwhile, experts said the country is headed for a budget crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How AI is likely to change Germany's job market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38a8956039a7d668826e9d5b9cd7f911173c62f665104e0f39f5b9bd011e09c9</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T05:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597--3a5b2bd9406d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The scale of the economic disruption caused by AI has led even conservative politicians to talk about universal basic income. But economists aren't convinced, and campaigners think we need to ask deeper questions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's 2027 budget: A record €561 billion and a mountain of debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:294bbca53f7c94036e619890a08b5398207178cb5052e68d4ab6d3e8d4980c49</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-_561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216--747b01c10ad0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-€561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2027 federal budget proposal has finally been hammered out and is set for a vote in parliament. What are the government's policy priorities in defense, infrastructure, the economy and social spending?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Holzer Prize awarded to Katja Gloger and DW's Jaafar Abdul Karim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a47d0d76b882cab74f84cbedf3c432f1ced14a9a3545c55dec5e613d7486299</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916--5a434ad9f59c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW journalist Jaafar Abdul Karim and Russia correspondent Katja Gloger have been awarded the prestigious Werner Holzer Prize for international journalism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy says security deal could go to referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:953e2e020135ee27609300e0862b0ccaaaecd95c438010e93e4d4d16970e54ef</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535--17ea05d7ca0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has broached the idea of Kyiv giving up the Donbas region in exchange for NATO membership, the Ukrainian president said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wolf Biermann at 90: The singer who defied East Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f27f675382402a7f7ee5e23b0f8b2ea6c89a6957331957c005ca276f07142f05</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297--17726feda083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">His life is a reflection of contemporary German history, addressed via his songs and sharp wit. At 90, he's as feisty as ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey uses espionage accusations to pressure government critics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:080df7873ba1e738