/><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts warn against revising Europe's security framework because they say it would mean granting Moscow its longstanding wish of renegotiating postwar security on the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What's going on with the polar vortex?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df8e9492c33e874e41b811cc466bcfc41be99e0c2b6cd86d661f217e879bafd</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105--6a28f0640609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Observations show the ring of fierce winds that rotate at the Earth's North Pole has changed direction. Scientists say it's a historic disruption and the earliest reversal on record. What could it mean for the weather?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey impasse as Russia threatens sanctions on Canada, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebce1a353b4ce9e5a072a7fac34f977dcd8554a47f19f344bd9cd8bf03205354</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676--52aad908ad79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany gives sweeping powers to police, intelligence services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dff8c122dccba71563e9938270e5b04f4f75cf2e61622822ed0157e65730449</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-police-intelligence-services/a-79941507--d8d4b64d3956.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-police-intelligence-services/a-79941507?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone sightings and cyberattacks have heightened security concerns. How are the police preparing to meet these challenges? And how do intelligence services plan to counter threats from both domestic and foreign sources?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f0b199cafda31aac409bfae55ac63e9fa7ff855596e4a3f57b47026cba0efba</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp has said midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament agrees on debt-laden 2027 budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47ae9456f9d7e0c56650ceb5ac79026b47dd05de4256e4aa0897458e0978290e</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897--be62c4ec3578.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget committee in the Bundestag worked into the night to sign off on next year's spending plans. These include levels of new debt only eclipsed once, at the height of the COVID pandemic. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia braces for massive protest against public media reform plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ba3e587347d4c21f960854935901aa3e0feb356d7a43befc8a480620c1a8acb</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533--a08ee7cdb27e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-tracked bill to cut public media funding has sparked strikes, rallies and fears for the independence of public broadcasting in Czechia. A massive protest is planned for Prague on Sunday.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could lack of money sink TFFF rainforest fund before it even launches?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ce451411ab893eab8d6be053b5cd9f033a127f6f03c11977a4db7234bce757c</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673--227abf2cebee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TFFF rainforest fund aims to make forest conservation more profitable than deforestation. But a lack of money may prevent it from getting off the ground.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian activist and Nobel Peace Prize winner Narges Mohammadi shares her story in memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ab8e2b40260dffb9f5d4cc58090d68f6a67f6c8a3b16485dd16d0696a1ffb0b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167--a983bd7e2dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Written and smuggled out of prison, the 2023 Nobel Prize laureate's memoir reveals the cost of defying Iran's regime and fighting for freedom.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders tussle over whom to send to Ukraine, Russia peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:993c4823a1a1a59b341632e54d497ca82ec19e85abd500e1dcb94f6d22a2b0a6</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468--127d08162dcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A seat at the table for Europe now appears likely following comments by a US envoy who just held talks with Putin. But who will take that seat remains unclear.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can the EU make it harder to trick consumers online?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64c5dd77ee6dc28a715744179bbc010a984eeac8a4f33fdd0e65f1c8388b083b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447--856c99598d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to curb subscription traps, misleading sales tactics and features that keep people scrolling. What would the proposed Digital Fairness Act change, and does it go far enough?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, affairs leave Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd087e8d5d781a68353847bc88b4e3cdbf97e3a57c1e990376fd88a51efcae8</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--e6a7da621d57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO over extramarital affairs. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>What are fossil fuels?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8feede44b63e3836545601dce94f72b204969414a9023570f3170c87f04e9939</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540--1920eabf4714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via