anything-and-why-it-s-important/a-79908787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doing nothing might be the ultimate brain hack. When you're bored, the brain goes into default mode network. It's not only healthy for you, but it may also shape the very essence of your identity.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aba3bb788085b93e71965ea0533d98eba0ac5e42140035a4904bfd9aaca3d2a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5928c786253c35dfacbdafb9ba0fd02bf1288b2b586408f4b16d8b831eb8bc61</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edc2d50430b91ea26bde9293bfd6273866f84b54fae3a1276eaee49c3c756a56</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8653c746808904868fed3882a9f8a5c2a78398ac19451a9650f120656140eb5f</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund's Felix Nmecha and the question of religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f36120b23d51b59c691959a355ce2fb95d9d7fcaab26725215f7da06aeffad83</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pag